# [< client_name >] — platform

The GitOps platform repo for **[< client_name >]** (`[< domain >]`), stamped from the
[platform factory](https://github.com/buildwithamaku/platform-template). Argo CD
reconciles everything under `clusters/` from this repo; after one bootstrap, every
change is a git commit — nothing is applied to the cluster by hand.

## Two planes
- **Plane 1 — infra** (`tofu/`): OpenTofu provisions the Kubernetes cluster
  (cloud = **[< cloud >]**). Run once per environment.
- **Plane 2 — GitOps** (`clusters/`): Argo CD runs everything else — ingress, TLS,
  secrets (External Secrets ← Infisical), the app database (CloudNativePG + PITR to
  R2), cache, observability, and the app(s) — from this repo. If it can run in the
  cluster, it is not in OpenTofu.

## Operating it
- **[`docs/RUNBOOK.md`](docs/RUNBOOK.md)** — onboarding, day-2, disaster recovery,
  incident response, secrets rotation, offboarding (tailored to this client's answers).
- **[`docs/APP-CONTRACT.md`](docs/APP-CONTRACT.md)** — what an app must do to deploy here.

## Layout
```
tofu/       # Plane 1 — cluster substrate (modules + per-env live roots)
clusters/   # Plane 2 — Argo CD app-of-apps + platform + apps
docs/       # RUNBOOK, APP-CONTRACT
.github/    # reusable delivery workflow (build-and-bump) + e2e gate
```

## Quick start
```bash
cd tofu/live/staging && tofu init && tofu apply   # Plane 1 → ./kubeconfig   (RUNBOOK §1.3)
export KUBECONFIG=$PWD/kubeconfig
./bootstrap.sh                                     # Plane 2 → Argo CD reconciles the rest (§1.4)
kubectl -n argocd get applications -w              # all Synced/Healthy (§1.5)
```
